Hi All,

This is just to confirm that rworldmap 1.3-1 has been up on CRAN for a week or so.
I'd recommend updating ( install.packages("rworldmap") ).

Main changes from the previous CRAN version are :
~ cleaner imports (loading should be quicker)
~ French Guiana separated from France
~ Western Sahara codes corrected
~ improved country to grid conversions
~ mapPies() fixed xlim ylim
~ Added line width option (lwd) for country boundaries in maps

More details here :
http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rworldmap/ChangeLog

I plan to get some more development in over the next month and will keep you posted.
Happy mapping,
Andy

