You can add custom legends using the legend() comand (I recommend reading the help documentation). This is what I did to add legends to my map (see https://gist.github.com/kgturner/5799785 and http://alienplantation.wordpress.com/2013/06/18/nuts-and-bolts-modern-maps-of-eurasia-in-r/ for more information on the map).

legend("bottomleft", c("Germination trial", "Broad CG","Maternal effects CG"),

       pch=c(1,19,15),  bg="white", title = "Sampled populations")

#location for legend, labels in the legend, symbols in the lengend, background color, title of legend

legend("topright", c("Invasive", "Native","Present, status unknown"), fill=c("#F8766D","#00BFC4", "cadetblue1"),

       title="Origin", bg="white")

kathryn

